      "why": "pipelined_m registers every m stages, cutting FF count (and thus power) versus fully pipelined while still delivering 1 result/cycle. The longer combinational path (m micro-rotations) lowers Fmax, so m=2-4 is the sweet spot where Fmax likely still exceeds 50 MHz. This family should dominate the low-power end of the front at comparable accuracy, since accuracy depends only on W/N/guards, not on m."
    }
