  "rationale": "The spec demands 50 MSPS throughput, which forces a 1-result/cycle architecture (pipelined or pipelined_m); iterative/unrolled_k are excluded by my fleet assignment and would also struggle to hit 50 MSPS without very high Fmax. The error constraint (<= 2^-12) is met by N~14-16 with W~16-18, so I center the search there. I split the budget between pipelined (baseline, highest Fmax, most FFs) and pipelined_m (fewer FFs, lower Fmax) to map the power/accuracy trade-off: pipelined_m should push the front toward lower power_index at the same accuracy, while pipelined covers the higher-Fmax / lower-latency corner. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small (0-2) since they add area/power with limited accuracy benefit at these widths; rounding is explored as a cheap accuracy lever. Both families share identical accuracy for the same W/N/guards, so the trade-off is purely power (FFs and Fmax) vs accuracy."
}

